### Account and session requests. Run the app with SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=local;
### the verification token is printed in the console log (local profile only).

@host = http://localhost:8080/api/v1

### Register (always 202, whether or not the address is taken)
POST {{host}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ann@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-battery" }

### Verify (paste the token from the console log)
POST {{host}}/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{ "token": "paste-token-from-the-log" }

### Log in: the response body has the access token, the refresh token comes as a cookie
# @name login
POST {{host}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ann@example.com", "password": "correct-horse-battery" }

### Refresh (needs the cookie and the custom header)
POST {{host}}/auth/refresh
X-Requested-With: ledgerly

### Log out
POST {{host}}/auth/logout
X-Requested-With: ledgerly

### Public signing keys
GET http://localhost:8080/.well-known/jwks.json
